%N A399175 Irregular triangle read by upward antidiagonals in which row n is the (finite) Goodstein trajectory of n.
%C A399175 The Goodstein trajectories of n >= 0 have lengths 1 (n=0), 2 (n=1), 4 (n=2), 6 (n=3, see A215409), about 10^121210694 (n=4, see A056193), ...
%C A399175 In the present triangle the rows are simply these trajectories. A296441 is a similar triangle, except that there the rows are extended with infinitely many zeros. In that triangle the rows are read by downward antidiagonals.
%H A399175 Alois P. Heinz, <a href="/A399175/b399175.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..165</a> (Antidiagonals n = 0..20)
%H A399175 N. J. A. Sloane, <a href="/A399175/a399175_1.jpg">The triangle with rows and columns labeled</a>
